   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Absorption and useful theorems"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Absorption: $A + AB = A$ and $A(A + B) = A$. Two very useful results: $A + \\overline{A}B = A + B$ and $A(\\overline{A} + B) = AB$. Every law has a dual, obtained by swapping + with · and 0 with 1. Simplifying an expression reduces the number of gates needed to build it."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "A + AB = A"
    },
    {
     "en": "A + A̅B = A + B"
    },
    {
     "en": "Duality: swap + ↔ · and 0 ↔ 1"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Absorption removes extra terms: A plus A B is just A. And A plus not A B becomes A plus B. Fewer terms mean fewer gates.",
    "kn": "ಹೀರಿಕೆ ನಿಯಮ ಹೆಚ್ಚುವರಿ ಪದಗಳನ್ನು ತೆಗೆಯುತ್ತದೆ: A + AB = A. ಮತ್ತು A + A̅B = A + B. ಕಡಿಮೆ ಪದಗಳು ಎಂದರೆ ಕಡಿಮೆ ದ್ವಾರಗಳು."
   },
   "formula": "A + \\overline{A}B = A + B"
